{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-03T01:26:12.886Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"43","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed in maskCPlusPlusOperatorCall, where this finding said the fix belonged. The mask preserved the width of the whole match but not of the operator's own name: 'operator=' (9 chars) collapsed to 'op' (2), and since names are sliced from unmasked source at the node's byte range, the slice read wrong bytes and every operator collapsed onto one 'op' — hence dropping bodyless overloads outright. The stand-in is now padded with '_' to the operator name's width ('op_______'), staying one identifier token so the slice returns the real spelling. Same technique as maskCPlusPlusConversionOperatorDecl. 'Ledger\u0026 operator=(const Ledger\u0026);' now yields Ledger.operator=, and =/==/!= stay distinct. Regression test verified failing without the fix; full suite green. Pushed to audit/lang-cpp-inclass-declarations (PR #177).","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1J004JEA1YG40ZNA1H5MBPY","targetId":"01M1J004JZ1NWZ84NBWGPMG2NR","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M15HKAZHNT2V832RRPJZ9R2Q"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
