{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-04T12:13:08.666Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"64","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed on the PR branch (3d02ff74). CONFIRMED: 'class Arena { void* operator new(size_t); void operator delete(void*); ... }' yielded only [class:Arena, method:Arena.Add] — the punctuation mask cannot match word-spelled operators, so they arrive as real operator_name nodes and were discarded outright. The operator_name branch now recovers them, gated on a token boundary and an 'operator' prefix that is not followed by an identifier byte. Mutation: the revert and the normalize-drop were killed (the latter by an added 'operator   co_await' whitespace case); two survivors were assessed as EQUIVALENT for every constructible input, since all C++ masks are length-preserving and a rewritten operator parses as an identifier rather than operator_name, so no mask can synthesise an 'operator' prefix. Both guards kept as defence-in-depth mirroring the sibling identifier branch, and flagged so a reviewer can decide.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1NPZSDZDH4GACCJB0T9D36Q","targetId":"01M1NPZSE3HZY3G1Z9S9GS62MB","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M15HKAZHNT2V832RRPJZ9R2Q"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-04T12:13:09.873Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"65","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed on the PR branch (3d02ff74). CONFIRMED in both directions: signatureNamesQualifiedMethod('int A\u003cstd::vector\u003cT\u003e\u003e::foo(int x)','A','foo') returned false where true is right (also A\u003cB\u003cC\u003cD\u003e\u003e\u003e, A\u003cmap\u003cK,V\u003e,list\u003cT\u003e\u003e, A\u003c...\u003cT\u003e \u003e), AND the inverse — 'int A\u003cB\u003cC\u003e::foo' with an UNBALANCED list wrongly returned true. Replaced the scan-to-first-'\u003e' with skipBalancedAngles, which depth-counts and reports whether the list actually closed. Mutation: 6 total; two initially survived and were killed by an added helper-contract test, and one was PROVED EQUIVALENT — when the list is unclosed the returned text still begins with '\u003c' (guaranteed by the caller's HasPrefix check), so the subsequent '::'+name match fails and the loop continues regardless. The explicit guard is kept as a statement of intent.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1NMX8ZDH2M5ZC2S3XAP1EQ6","targetId":"01M1NMX8ZPKK5Z393RZBV6SZG5","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M15HKAZHNT2V832RRPJZ9R2Q"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-04T12:13:11.074Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"66","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"REFUTED — the premise is false, verified live rather than by inspection. walkEntitiesScoped does 'childScope = entity.Name', which REPLACES the scope rather than appending, so a C++ member's QualifiedName is always exactly Container.Name and containerName() returns the bare immediate container — never 'ns.A' or 'Outer.Inner'. Evidence: a namespaced member gives qn='Ledger.Add' against definition signature 'int ns::Ledger::Add(int) const'; a nested one gives qn='Inner.Add' against 'int Outer::Inner::Add(int) const'; signatureNamesQualifiedMethod returns true for both. End-to-end, a resolvable receiver inside a namespace produces the CALLS edge correctly, so the redirect already works. No code changed.\n\nTwo REAL but different gaps were found while refuting, both pre-existing (main has no in-class method symbols at all, so neither is a regression here) and both in RECEIVER-TYPE RESOLUTION rather than in the container comparison this finding names: an 'Outer::Inner*' receiver resolves its targetID to Outer so the lookup fails, and an 'ns::Ledger*' receiver does not reach the method lookup at all in a three-file build though it works in a two-file inline build.","to":"dismissed"},"reviewId":"01M1NMX8ZDH2M5ZC2S3XAP1EQ6","targetId":"01M1NMX8ZJ8763RAT80QG6NEGY","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M15HKAZHNT2V832RRPJZ9R2Q"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
